From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: unom <packages@unom.io>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:57:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 51/52] layer: let Proton's fullscreen hack scale a game in its
 own format

Proton's fullscreen hack scales a DPI-scaled window in the game's
process. The game draws into images of its own format, and a compute
pass writes them to a storage-only BGRA8 swapchain. The pass views every
game image as BGRA8 sRGB, all an X11 surface offers, and encodes what it
samples to sRGB.

This layer offers more formats. A 10-bit HDR10 image was read as 8-bit
BGRA and came out as noise, an RGBA8 image had red and blue swapped, and
any HDR picture was cut to an 8-bit swapchain.

From such a swapchain to its last view, the layer corrects what Proton
creates on that thread. An HDR colorspace gets the format the layer
offers with it. Each view of a game image gets that image's format, sRGB
where it has one. Where it has none, the two sRGB constants in Proton's
pass are replaced so that it stores what it samples. A BGRA8 game gets
the calls it got before.
---
 layer/VkLayer_FROG_gamescope_wsi.cpp | 216 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 215 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

